keyframes.prompt_template:
Generate a high-quality {aspect_ratio} photorealistic vertical image for this scene end frame. This is keyframe K{scene_index} of {total_scenes}.

CRITICAL CAMERA LOCK: This keyframe must use the EXACT SAME camera position, height, angle, tilt, focal length, lens feel, and horizon line as every other keyframe in this sequence. The camera is a physical tripod bolted to one fixed spot in the backyard. It has not moved, shifted, rotated, elevated, lowered, zoomed, or reframed since keyframe K1. The composition and framing must be pixel-identical to all previous keyframes. Only the environment and worker state may differ between keyframes.

CRITICAL: If this is keyframe K1, it must use the SAME camera position, angle, pool, house, fence, and patio as all subsequent keyframes. K1 is NOT a separate establishing shot from a different viewpoint. It shows the same fixed-tripod view of the same property, only in its initial neglected state.

CRITICAL PROPERTY IDENTITY LOCK: The house, fence, patio/deck, pool shape, and all permanent structures must look EXACTLY the same as in keyframe K1. The house architecture (style, color, roof, windows, wall material), fence (type, height, material, layout), patio/deck (material, shape, position), and pool (shape, size, position in frame) are all permanently locked. Do not change, replace, or alter any of these elements. The property in this keyframe must be unmistakably the same property as in K1.

CRITICAL MONOTONIC PROGRESS: All areas that were cleaned or restored in previous keyframes must remain clean and restored in this keyframe. No previously cleaned section of the pool, deck, patio, or yard may appear dirty or messy again. Progress only moves forward, never backward.

