This frame must preserve the exact same static camera position and framing as every other keyframe in the sequence, including K1. Treat the camera as physically bolted in place in one backyard. Use a medium-wide readable exterior shot from a slightly elevated angle that shows the pool work zone prominently and enough surrounding property context to lock the location. The pool area must be large and easy to read. The environment must look materially more advanced than before across the whole work area and surrounding yard, not just through a new worker pose. Preserve the same backyard identity, same house and fence layout, same landscaping anchors, and same pool identity. Keep the same recognizable original pool shell throughout and visibly improve the whole yard too. Show believable one-man progress, realistic materials, realistic water behavior, realistic tool logic, and tasteful luxury finishing. No text, numbers, subtitles, logos, labels, or watermarks.
